{"id":"v8","level":4,"levelName":"The verb system","n":13,"of":15,"title":"Roots that misbehave","titleHe":"גְּזָרוֹת","goal":"Read verbs whose roots contain נ, ו or ה and don't follow the tables.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"The tables you've learned describe strong roots — three solid consonants. Some roots contain a letter that won't stay put, and those are among the commonest verbs in the language, so they have to be met head-on."},{"type":"weak","id":"pe-nun","item":{"id":"pe-nun","he":"פ״נ","en":"roots beginning with נ","why":"The נ vanishes into the next letter, which takes a dagesh instead.","verb":{"root":"נ־פ־ל","inf":"לִפֹּל","en":"to fall"},"forms":[{"label":"he falls","he":"נוֹפֵל","note":"present keeps the נ"},{"label":"he fell","he":"נָפַל","note":"past keeps it too"},{"label":"he will fall","he":"יִפֹּל","note":"the נ is gone; פ doubles"},{"label":"to fall","he":"לִפֹּל","note":"same in the infinitive"}]}},{"type":"weak","id":"ayin-vav","item":{"id":"ayin-vav","he":"ע״ו","en":"hollow roots","why":"The middle letter is a vowel, so there are only two consonants to hear.","verb":{"root":"ק־ו־ם","inf":"לָקוּם","en":"to get up"},"forms":[{"label":"he gets up","he":"קָם","note":"one syllable — no middle letter"},{"label":"she gets up","he":"קָמָה","note":""},{"label":"he got up","he":"קָם","note":"past and present look alike"},{"label":"I got up","he":"קַמְתִּי","note":""},{"label":"he will get up","he":"יָקוּם","note":"the vav surfaces as u"}]}},{"type":"weak","id":"lamed-he","item":{"id":"lamed-he","he":"ל״ה","en":"roots ending in ה","why":"The final ה drops before most endings, and the vowel before it shifts.","verb":{"root":"ק־נ־ה","inf":"לִקְנוֹת","en":"to buy"},"forms":[{"label":"he buys","he":"קוֹנֶה","note":""},{"label":"she buys","he":"קוֹנָה","note":"not קונת"},{"label":"they buy","he":"קוֹנִים","note":"the ה is gone"},{"label":"he bought","he":"קָנָה","note":""},{"label":"I bought","he":"קָנִיתִי","note":"ה becomes י"},{"label":"to buy","he":"לִקְנוֹת","note":"infinitive ends ־וֹת"}]}},{"type":"tip","body":"Don't memorise rules for these. Learn the handful of frequent verbs in each family as words, and the pattern will settle by itself."}],"vocab":[{"he":"נוֹפֵל","en":"falls","translit":"nofel"},{"he":"נוֹסֵעַ","en":"travels","translit":"nose'a"},{"he":"קָם","en":"gets up","translit":"kam"},{"he":"שָׁר","en":"sings","translit":"shar"},{"he":"קוֹנֶה","en":"buys","translit":"kone"},{"he":"רוֹאֶה","en":"sees","translit":"ro'e"},{"he":"עוֹשֶׂה","en":"does, makes","translit":"ose"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["world","metre","culture","falls"],"correct":3,"prompt":"נוֹפֵל","translit":"nofel"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["tries","well done","travels","feeling"],"correct":2,"prompt":"נוֹסֵעַ","translit":"nose'a"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["said","homeland","gets up","people, men"],"correct":2,"prompt":"קָם","translit":"kam"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["roof","bathroom, bath","sings","plays"],"correct":2,"prompt":"שָׁר","translit":"shar"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["late","Mishnah, teaching","silence, stillness","buys"],"correct":3,"prompt":"קוֹנֶה","translit":"kone"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["explains","without","student (m.)","sees"],"correct":3,"prompt":"רוֹאֶה","translit":"ro'e"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["dad","thank you","does, makes","ring"],"correct":2,"prompt":"עוֹשֶׂה","translit":"ose"},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["רוֹאֶה","עוֹשֶׂה","קוֹנֶה","נוֹסֵעַ"],"correct":2,"say":"קוֹנֶה","he":true},{"type":"read","he":"קוֹנֶה","translit":"kone","en":"buys"},{"type":"choice","q":"get up (ע״ו) — she gets up","options":["נָפַל","יִפֹּל","נוֹפֵל","קָמָה"],"correct":3,"he":true,"why":"The middle letter is a vowel, so there are only two consonants to hear."},{"type":"choice","q":"buy (ל״ה) — to buy","options":["נָפַל","נוֹפֵל","לִקְנוֹת","יִפֹּל"],"correct":2,"he":true,"why":"The final ה drops before most endings, and the vowel before it shifts."},{"type":"match","pairs":[["נוֹפֵל","falls"],["נוֹסֵעַ","travels"],["קָם","gets up"],["שָׁר","sings"],["קוֹנֶה","buys"]]},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “travels”?","options":["נוֹסֵעַ","הַיּוֹם","בְּמֶשֶׁךְ","תַּאֲרִיךְ"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"buy (ל״ה) — he buys","options":["יִפֹּל","נוֹפֵל","קוֹנֶה","נָפַל"],"correct":2,"he":true,"why":"The final ה drops before most endings, and the vowel before it shifts."},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “gets up”?","options":["אֵבֶל","מָנוֹעַ","קָם","בֵּית קָפֶה"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"type","q":"Write “sings” in Hebrew","answer":"שָׁר","hint":"shar"}]}